// that the mullions and the transom stand proud of it. Panes are 6 cm thick
// and take a flat light level rather than a baked one: a sheet of glass has no
// shading of its own to speak of, and a level that holds still across the face
// is also the cheapest thing to blend, since it collapses to one multiplier for
// the whole pane instead of a step per pixel.
//
// alpha keeps three tenths of the pane and lets seven through, so the city
// reads as the city with a tint over it rather than through a curtain. The
// level and the alpha are separate: the level is how bright the glass itself
// is, the alpha is how much of the city survives it.
